    {
      "name": "Guild Chat (WebSocket)",
      "description": "`WS {{baseUrl}}/guilds/{guildId}/chat` - real-time guild chat.\n\nPostman's collection file format (v2.1) cannot store WebSocket requests, so this one has to be created inside the Postman app:\n\n1. New -> WebSocket Request\n2. URL: ws://localhost:8087/guilds/<paste a guildId>/chat\n3. Connect. The server immediately sends the existing history:\n   { \"type\": \"history\", \"messages\": [] }\n4. Send this JSON message:\n   { \"authorId\": \"u-owner-1\", \"message\": \"hello guild\" }\n5. The server stamps it and broadcasts it to every connected member:\n   { \"authorId\": \"u-owner-1\", \"message\": \"hello guild\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-22T12:11:03.692Z\" }\n\nRules: connecting to an unknown guildId closes the socket with code 1008. Only existing members of the guild may post - anyone else gets { \"error\": \"author is not a member of this guild\" }.\n\nTo demonstrate the broadcast, open two WebSocket tabs on the same guild and send from one of them.",
      "item": []
    }
